rror payload across that axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:21:#     non-bg top-row cells are spread across the bar field and each is locally tied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:84:    Legends are distributed across the top row: each legend is a one-column stack\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:184:    distributed across the bar field instead of forming one contiguous cluster.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/3/code.py:56:#      r=c, so the \"up branch vs down branch\" contrast is actually visible across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/3/code.py:60:#      generator. This removes messy layered intersections that would hide the one-sided\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/3/code.py:164:    # crosses it. Valid generated data keeps segments disjoint, so this is usually one branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D3/2/code.py:57:#      Across 2-4 examples a human can see that beam thickness tracks blob size, not the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c3d4a41/D14/2/code.py:58:#       Distinct colors across the four columns make the recoloring rule easy to compare by eye.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/2/code.py:273:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/2/code.py:413:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D15/1/code.py:34:# same hollow cross plus repeated colored corner hints, and the resulting spiral bends\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D15/1/code.py:200:    - bg = 0 (black). One hollow teal cross plus some colored path markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D15/1/code.py:204:    - Turtles still launch from the four cross tips and still use the seed task's right-turn / straight / left candidate ordering with the same 2/1 step schedule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/2/code.py:39:#      obvious across fe