/code.py:14:      A cross is {center, up, down, left, right}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:15:      The two cross centers are the diagonal corners of the rectangle to fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:16:      The crosses stay visible in the output; only the rectangle between their centers is recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:20:      Suppose marker color 4 has crosses centered at (2,3) and (7,9).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:27:      - that logic would fail because a symmetric cross has no L orientation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:30:      - recognize each 5-pixel component as a cross and read its center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:35:      The bounding box of all marker pixels is no longer the fill rectangle because each cross extends\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:41:      Keeping exactly two identical crosses per active color limits free-form ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:58:      - The fill rectangle must come from detected cross centers, not from extremal marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:59:      - Since all active markers are now cross-pairs, the block branch is removed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:61:      - Every non-noop legend marker color has exactly two disconnected 5-pixel cross components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:72:      Because same-color cross components are disconnected, component-based center extraction is stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:155:def _cross_center(comp: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:156:    \"\"\"Return the center of an exact 5-pixel cross component, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/c